  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following a widespread flight grounding that occurred on Friday and affected over one million passengers, federal officials are intensifying efforts to modernize the United States air traffic control system. Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy is currently petitioning for $50 billion in funding to execute critical FAA hardware and software upgrades. While the exact root cause of the recent system glitch remains under investigation, some retired air traffic controllers have pointed toward potential router failures as a contributing factor. In response to the disruption, a so-called tiger team has been assembled to prevent similar nationwide ground stops. The incident has drawn significant legislative attention, with members of the Senate calling for a formal pause on planned modernization efforts until the current issues are fully understood. Ongoing travel difficulties have led to varied passenger experiences, including large groups arranging alternative ground transportation to reach their destinations.",
